comments.body:
nit: I would expand the comment a little bit, it makes sense to explain why we are guarding with `m_from_snapshot_blockhash`, and also why `GetPruneHeight` makes sense even on non-pruned nodes:
```
// Check that the blocks to disconnect are available and protect them from pruning.
// They can be missing either because they were pruned, or because this is a snapshot
// chainstate whose historical blocks have not been downloaded or connected yet.
// We use GetPruneHeight in either case, as it scans down from the tip and returns the
// highest block missing body or undo data
```

